    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="1001" n="887" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51/169: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schuyler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-26T13:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26, 1922—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>56. The President and I are officially informed that the loan contract has been
                    signed in New York between Keilhauer representing the Government of Salvador and
                    Mr. Keith.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d786-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d786-f1" n="7" xml:id="d786-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister had advised the Department, June 22, that Salvador had authorized
                    Mr. René Keilhauer to sign modified loan contract with Mr. Minor C. Keith, and
                    that the latter would himself make the loan (file no. 816.51/168). The contract
                    was signed on June 24 (file no. 816.51/182).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
